reated  open source connectors and we have put  them in github it's accessible to  everyone  using those open source connectors users  like yourself can  ingest metadata from hive oracle  sql server teradata redshift mysql  postgresql the list continues to grow we  have also added vertica green plum  and as you can see we can also ingest  with these connectors  you can also ingest technical metadata  from bi tools like looker and tableau  the end result is that data catalog  gives you a unified view  of all your data assets a single pane of  glass  to find them all right a little bit  about the data catalog architecture  because one of the question that often  comes up is that you know how robust is  this service how global is this service  how scalable is this service  so we have launched data catalog nga we  did that at the end of april  we have launched the service in 23  different regions  and multi regions so it's a global  service and it provides metadata  residency at rest  and the big there are many building  blocks and the three big building  blocks are the real-time and batch  sinkers  that bring metadata from various sources  and put it in the data catalog  then the metadata store itself which  stores all the metadata in the data  so metadata store is just a transaction  store we  use spanner to build the infrastructure  as you know spanner is a globally  distributed  strongly consistent database to a very  solid foundation  we also leverage the same google search  technology that powers gmail  and google drive and that gives us  search with access control built into it  gmail as you know has more than billion  users and so we know that this is a very  scalable technology  so data catalog is built on this very  strong foundation  in terms of innovation what we really  introduce that is new here is the  concept of structure tags  so the traditional catalogs usually  enable tags  usually enable users to put on tags but  those stacks are simple text strings 