adata that users need  access to and there is no easy way of  providing this  you know people often ask me what's the  competition for the data catalog and  the answer is interestingly you know  google sheets excel spread  excel sheets wiki pages confluence pages  typically the metadata is spread all  over the place and there is no  easy way to make it available online  make it searchable  and our structure tags enable users to  exactly that  have another example here for data  quality now often one of the big  challenges analysts face  is that they discover a data asset but  they have no idea as to what's the  quality of this data is it actually  approved is it usable is it mostly  null how is what's the cardinality  what's the mean max medium  data catalog tags enable you to compute  all the data quality metrics and make it  available as business data  the pii tags are kind of self-evident  here right  so in this example i have two fields in  the pi tag one is  the has pii which is of type boolean and  it's set to true here  the second is type pii for the second  column it says hey  it's an ssn for the fourth column it  indicates that it's an email address  so the structure tags provide a very  powerful flexible and generic way to tap  all kinds of business metadata and make  it available to your users  so let's talk a little bit more about  the structure tanks  if there is a structure to the tag there  has to be a way to specify the structure  so we have the concept of templates we  didn't want to call it schema so it  could in terms  so on the left i show an example of a  template where you can say okay  and by the way all of this is completely  customizable so  if you as a user want to create a tag  template  and put five or six or twenty fields in  it you can do that  so in this example i have this field  called approved by data awareness  and it is of type boolean and then i  have data classification which is of  type enumerated and  in this enumerated type f