ed with  iam  security is built into data catalog from  the get go  so we have two personas here we have  data governor persona and let's say in  this case  data governor has full access to data  assets in project a b and c  and we have another persona data analyst  and data analyst  has full access to data assets in  project a but  metadata read only access to data sets  in project b  and no access at all the project c even  though  all the metadata resides in the search  index  when the data analyst looks for data  assets they see a different view  because in the 500 milliseconds that we  try to return results and we do like 98  percent of the time  we run probably hundred thousand apple  checks or access control checks  to figure out who can see what and this  is a really really important point for  many of our customers especially the  financial customers banks etc  because security is paramount and you  cannot compromise that and so  as i mentioned we have it built into it  now building  further on top of that security  framework  the tags themselves are also access  controlled  right so in this scenario we have data  governor persona  who has access to three different tags  and the data analyst persona has access  to only two of those stacks  because in many cases we have seen  customers especially the data governance  team  create tags where they put sensitive  information and they do not want others  to see this  and data catalog enables you to do that  so even the tags are  also under access control now the next  thing that i want to mention is that  ev you know we believe in a very open  system we believe that it's your  metadata you can do  whatever you want to do if you want to  bring in metadata from other systems  or you want to take metadata out we  enable you to do that  and in order for you to do this in bulk  as in bringing in large amounts of  metadata from outside  into our search index or take out the  metadata we enable  apis and we support sev