eeded to develop our own solution  as the catalog has moved to the  um to the general access phase  new functionality has been added  including  including automatic tagging and tagging  of sensitive information  we would like to start using that in the  next iteration of our products  following is a short demo of the product  that we built  using data catalog as our engine  hi and welcome to data predator data  data is an application that was created  on gcp  which relies on the gcp data catalog  for its core functionality data verdega  allows  users to use an intuitive and  user-friendly interface to try and find  all of the datasets available to them  and to do further simple analysis where  possible  when someone logs into data bodega  they'll be able to see  all of the cat space stats split out by  category  into different sections each one of the  files in each section  consists of a data set users can also  split  by sectors regions or style  the other way that people can search the  data is by looking at the intelligence  search on the left hand side here they  can enter a keyword  or if they know the table name or data  set the names of those  table names or data sets or they can do  a filter search  the filter search allows people to use  commonly  thought of tags and use those to do  searches  for this demo we're going to do a search  using intelligent search  i'm going to look for some of this data  this is data from the last publicly  available census  in the us as you can see we've got two  data sets the postal codes and the  we click on geospatial postal codes it  will open up the data set  and show me all of the tables available  there as you can see there's a near  single data table available  if i click on that on the right hand  side you will notice that we now see  a preview of the table as well as some  information that allows the user to  understand how fresh the data is and  also if they need permission to the data  in gcp and bigquery what project name to  ask for permission for  you can see that we can also show people  the top 50 rows of  each dataset that is available this is  refreshed  on a nightly basis and the only point of  this is to allow people to have an  idea of what the data set looks like  what kind of numbers are involved etc  you can also download this data as a csv  if needed  the other tab available here is the  analysis tab  if you click on here and the dataset has  time series data  there will be some simple graphing that  can be possible  you can also however open the data  directly in bigquery  if you have access already in tableau  or you can download the data dictionary  if  that's available the way we created this  application is we went into data um data  bodega  project in dcp we called it mosaic  and we went and created a bunch of data  tags  tag templates now the reason we created  so many  was that we needed to have multi-select  on some of our  tags such as region or country  and the only way to do that was to  create a region or country tag template  and have boolean yes or no on there  fortunately we were able to work with  google  to help us create the tag templates in  a format in excel which we were able to  then just upload into  gcp using python this made things a lot  easier and quicker than creating the tag  templates  on the front end we then went through  all of our data sets in bigquery  and tagged all of them using these tag  templates  the next step is to start auto tagging  datasets as they come in and are  onboarded using various data  data attributes that are made available  to us at the point of onboarding  this is a quick foray into what can be  built using  data catalog we've found it incredibly  useful to be able to go in  and connect and  allow users to go in and search for data  without knowing the name of the dataset  or knowing particular attributes of the  dataset and only knowing  roughly the topic that they're looking  for we hope to work furthe