ed with  iam  security is built into data catalog from  the get go  so we have two personas here we have  data governor persona and let's say in  this case  data governor has full access to data  assets in project a b and c  and we have another persona data analyst  and data analyst  has full access to data assets in  project a but  metadata read only access to data sets  in project b  and no access at all the project c even  though  all the metadata resides in the search  index  when the data analyst looks for data  assets they see a different view  because in the 500 milliseconds that we  try to return results and we do like 98  percent of the time  we run probably hundred thousand apple  checks or access control checks  to figure out who can see what and this  is a really really important point for  many of our customers especially the  financial customers banks etc  because security is paramount and you  cannot compromise that and so  as i mentioned we have it built into it  now building  further on top of that security  framework  the tags themselves are also access  controlled  right so in this scenario we have data  governor persona  who has access to three different tags  and the data analyst persona has access  to only two of those stacks  because in many cases we have seen  customers especially the data governance  team  create tags where they put sensitive  information and they do not want others  to see this  and data catalog enables you to do that  so even the tags are  also under access control now the next  thing that i want to mention is that  ev you know we believe in a very open  system we believe that it's your  metadata you can do  whatever you want to do if you want to  bring in metadata from other systems  or you want to take metadata out we  enable you to do that  and in order for you to do this in bulk  as in bringing in large amounts of  metadata from outside  into our search index or take out the  metadata we enable  apis and we support seven language  libraries  so that you can create all the action  behind  every ui there is an api call so  everything is available through the api  and many of our customers actually have  their own front ends also and they use  the api to power the back end because  this is a much more scalable and  performing backup  and at this point i would like to  invite shruti from blackrock  to share her experience using data  catalog  the reasons why they chose to partner  with google and  how they achieve their objectives  you hi i'm shutti taka i work in active  equities at blackrock and i'm head of  vendor data and alphabet  i'm also the google administrator for  our google cloud instance in my team  so why data catalog well when we started  our journey  bringing alternative data into into  blackrock  and making it available for our  investors to use in their research and  analysis  we started to find that the data that  was coming in was very different to the  more  traditional financial data that already  existed within blackrock  within the data structures that were  made available to us  so what we were seeing were lots of very  dynamic  schemas lots of different formats and  vendors and working with vendors that  really didn't  connect with financial industry as a  rule  so the data was coming in lots of  different  file types as well on the other side  we had a spectrum of users we had people  both geographically diverse  from san francisco to hong kong from  sydney to london as well as people who  had different levels of comfortableness  with the with how to get to the data  we had people who are very very  comfortable just going into a server  going to a cli environment finding the  file that they need pulling it and  analyzing it  on the other side we had lots of users  who really needed that interface that  front end  which allowed them to go in and search  for  data using keywords or tags  and then be able to find that data and  then  work with it what we found was that we  really weren't seeing  something that could help us with both  of these  issues within blackrock and so we  decided to  go and talk to our colleagues at google  cloud to see if there was  um something that they could help us  with  so we started talking to google cloud in  2018  and we explained to them what we were  trying to do  and luckily for us at that time checker  was just putting  data catalog into alpha  so we were able to get in there and talk  to sheker and his team  and explain what we were trying to do  and he showed us  what that it was possible to find a  solution using  a google data catalog  because the catalog was in alpha when we  started working with  uh with google cloud it was it was  possible for us to both  help shape the product and find a  solution that would work for us  in tandem one of the great things about  the data catalog  is that it's really well integrated into  the google cloud ecosystem  so when you're looking at one  part of this puzzle which is the data  catalog you're not then having to build  uh apis or build connections in to  other parts of google it's already  connected to bigquery it's already  connected to storage  and compute so it's quite easy  for us to be able to come up with an  integrated  and complex front end which would really  provide our users a really powerful way  to find and analyze data  we were also able to very simply create  uh templates both on the front end to  start with and then as our templates  became more complicated  we worked with sheker and the team to um  put our templates into an excel file  which we could then upload directly via  python  this actually made our lives a lot  easier  and we were able to create tags as we  wanted them we were able to say okay  well  we would like asset management as a tag  we would also like uh different sectors  as tags and we were able to put them in  there wasn't anything that was pre  uh pre-created which really gave us the  freedom that  we needed to develop our own solution  as the catalog has moved to the  um to the general access phase  new functionality has been added  including  including automatic tagging and tagging  of sensitive information  we would like to start using that in the  next iteration of our products  following is a short demo of the product  that we built  using data catalog as our engine  hi and welcome to data predator data  data is an application that was created  on gcp  which relies on the gcp data catalog  for its core functionality data verdega  allows  users to use an intuitive and  user-friendly interface to try and find  all of the datasets available to them  and to do further simple analysis where  possible  when someone logs into data bodega  they'll be able to see  all of the cat space stats split out by  category  into different sections each one of the  files in each section  consists of a data set users can also  split  by sectors regions or style  the other way that people can search the  data is by looking at the intelligence  search on the left hand side here they  can enter a keyword  or if they know the table name or data  set the names of those  table names or data sets or they can do  a filter search  the filter search allows people to use  commonly  thought of tags and use those to do  searches  for this demo we're going to do a search  using intelligent search  i'm going to look for some of this data  this is data from the last publicly  available census  in the us as you can see we've got two  data sets the postal codes and the  we click on geospatial postal codes it  will open up the data set  and show me all of the tables available  there as you can see there's a near  single data table available  if i click on that on the right hand  side you will notice that we now see  a preview of the table as well as some  information that allows the user to  understand how fresh the data is and  also if they need permission to the data  in gcp and bigquery what project name to  ask for permission for  you can see that we can also show people  the top 50 rows of  each dataset that is available this is  refreshed  on a nightly basis and the only point of  this is to allow people to have an  idea of what the data set looks like  what kind of numbers are involved etc  you can also download this data as a csv  if needed  the other tab available here is the  analysis tab  if you click on here and the dataset has  time series data  there will be some simple graphing that  can be possible  you can also however open the data  directly in bigquery  if you have access already in tableau  or you can download the data dictionary  if  that's available the way we created this  application is we went into data um data  bodega  project in dcp we called it mosaic  and we went and created a bunch of data  tags  tag templates now the reason we created  so many  was that we needed to have multi-select  on some of our  tags such as region or country  and the only way to do that was to  create a region or country tag template  and have boolean yes or no on there  fortunately we were able to work with  google  to help us create the tag templates in  a format in excel which we were able to  then just upload into  gcp using python this made things a lot  easier and quicker than creating the tag  templates  on the front end we then went through  all of our data sets in bigquery  and tagged all of them using these tag  templates  the next step is to start auto tagging  datasets as they come in and are  onboarded using various data  data attributes that are made available  to us at the point of onboarding  this is a quick foray into what can be  built using  data catalog we've found it incredibly  useful to be able to go in  and connect and  allow users to go in and search for data  without knowing the name of the dataset  or knowing particular attributes of the  dataset and only knowing  roughly the topic that they're looking  for we hope to work further with google  to create more functionality and more  depth to  our product using data catalog thank you  shruti for that wonderful presentation  and and the demo so what are the next  things you can do as a user  the first thing i want to point out is  that you can launch data catalog  right away there is no setup required  data catalog indexes all the metadata in  the background continuously  so all you need to do is to go to this  particular link the  console.cloud.google.com go to data  catalog  you can select a project that you want  to start using just enable the api  and all the data assets are already  discovered into you  just with a simple keyword search or the  powerful search language  you can also use dlp to auto tag pii  data in data catalog  the dlp integration is available through  the dlpu-1  it is also available through the api and  this link gives you the details of how  to do this  to tag pii data at the table level  as well as polymer and lastly  if you are one of the users who has data  scattered in all these different silos  and you're finding it really really hard  to discover those data assets  you can use one of our connectors  and all the connectors are listed in the  google's github repo  you can download them their open source  connectors and you can start using them  right away happy data discovery journey
 

